statement:
You are given `root`, the root of a binary search tree whose values are all distinct (it may be empty). Rewire the tree's own nodes into a **circular, sorted, doubly linked list** and return the node holding the smallest value:

- reuse each node's `left` field as the link to the previous (smaller) node and its `right` field as the link to the next (larger) node;
- the list wraps around: the smallest node's `left` points to the largest node, and the largest node's `right` points to the smallest;
- work in place: create no new nodes, so every node of the tree appears in the list exactly once;
- for an empty tree, return `null`.

Each case is written as `[root]`: the tree as a level-order array with `null` for missing children. Your function receives the root node object. The result is shown as the values met by starting at the returned node and following `right` once around the circle; the judge also checks that every `left` link points back to the previous node.

validator:
function validate([root]) {
  if (!Array.isArray(root)) return 'root is a level-order array with null for missing children.';
  if (root.length > 0 && root[0] === null) return 'An empty tree is written as [].';
  const values = root.filter(v => v !== null);
  if (values.length > 2000) return 'The tree has at most 2000 nodes.';
  if (values.some(v => !Number.isInteger(v) || v < -1000 || v > 1000)) return 'Node values are whole numbers from -1000 to 1000.';
  if (new Set(values).size !== values.length) return 'Node values must be unique.';
  // range[i] holds the open interval the value at position i must fall in to keep the search-tree order.
  const range = [[-Infinity, Infinity]];
  for (let i = 0; i < root.length; i++) {
    if (range[i] === undefined) return 'Every value after the root needs a parent in the level-order array.';
    const value = root[i];
    if (value === null) continue;
    const [low, high] = range[i];
    if (value <= low || value >= high) return 'The tree must be a binary search tree.';
    range.push([low, value], [value, high]);
  }
  return null;
}

